Subject: [PATCH 70/74] Meridian: the command bar reads text typed in the wrong
 keyboard layout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"ghbdtn" offers "привет", "пщщпду" offers "google" (Russian ЙЦУКЕН and
US QWERTY): when the other layout's letters read far more like its language
than the typed ones (no English vowels, letter frequencies), or match a
popular site or an open tab's host. A row above the suggestions; ⇥ or a
click puts it in the field.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
